[00:08.92]More and more people think that life is better in the city than the countryside.
[00:14.70]For the first time in history more than 50% of the world’s population lives in urban areas.
[00:22.40]However, there are still many groups of people who live in some of the wildest places on the planet.
[00:29.94]The Kalahari is a large area of bush land in southern Africa.
[00:35.74]It has two parts.
[00:37.68]The south part is drier than the north and plants do not grow there very well.
[00:43.82]Every year at the end of summer it rains and the land becomes more beautiful than at other times of the year.
[00:51.74]But the grass and the bushes soon get dry and turn brown again.
[00:56.72]Life there is difficult.
[00:59.30]The San are a group of people who live in the Kalahari.
[01:03.64]They live in huts, eat wild animals – even lions – plants and berries.
[01:10.10]They are very good with bows and arrows, and use them for hunting.
[01:15.38]Up in the mountains of central Papua New Guinea is the Chimbu Province.
[01:21.08]This jungle area is one of the world’s most remote places.
[01:25.90]It is also home to Mt Wilhelm, the highest mountain on the island.
[01:31.28]Several different tribes live in the valleys between the mountains.
[01:35.72]One of these is the Chimbu skeleton dancers.
[01:39.70]They paint skeletons onto their bodies.
[01:42.52]This makes them look scarier and it frightens other people away from their land.
[01:49.10]The Yamal Peninsula in northern Siberia is one and a half times bigger than France.
[01:56.12]It is frozen for much of the year and temperatures can reach -50°C in the winter.
[02:03.28]But this area is home to a tribe of about 10,000 people called the Nenets.
[02:09.58]The Nenets are nomadic, meaning they frequently move from one place to another.
[02:15.92]Each year around 300,000 reindeer move around the land and the Nenets always go with them.
[02:24.74]The recent discovery of gas in the area means more people than before are visiting the Yamal.
[02:31.30]So the Nenets now have more contact with the outside world.
[02:36.86]The Bayan-Ölgii Province is the highest part of Mongolia.
[02:41.90]It is a wild area with many mountains, lakes, forests and rivers.
[02:47.42]It is also home to the Kazakh golden eagle hunters.
[02:52.02]These people travel around the mountains and use eagles to hunt for foxes and other small animals.
[02:59.48]When boys turn 13, they can become golden eagle hunters.
[03:04.52]However, they have to be stronger than most boys their age because they have to show that they can carry the weight of an eagle.
[03:12.66]There are about 100,000 Kazakh people, but only around 250 of them are golden eagle hunters.
